    "lawCode": "Amd §§3001-b & 3001-c, Ed L",
    "lawSection": "Education Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8615A\n\nSPONSOR: MAY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the education law, in relation to first aid certif-\nication for coaches and staff of high school athletics\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to allow people with physical disabilities\nto coach school athletic teams that are prevented from doing so due to\nan inability to perform CPR as a result of their physical disability.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nThis bill would allow a teacher or person who is unable to hold a valid\ncertificate of completion of a course of study in first aid knowledge\nand skills due to a physical disability to coach any extra-class athlet-\nic activity if there is another teacher or person employed by the school\nsystem who holds a valid certificate of completion and is present at all\ntimes during the extra-class athletic activity including but not limited\nto practices, scrimmages, and during competitions.\n\nThe A-print of this legislation clarifies its applicability.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nUnder the current provisions of the Education Law people with physical\ndisabilities that cannot perform CPR and other life saving measures are\nprevented from becoming a head coach of a school athletic team.\n\nThis bill enables a person with such physical disabilities to serve as a\nhead coach provided certain safeguards are met to ensure that if a\nmedical incident arises it can be promptly dealt with by a qualified\nindividual paired with the head coach. Specifically, a person with a\nphysical disability that cannot currently qualify to coach may coach any\nextra-class athletic activity if there is another person or staff\nemployed by the school system who holds a valid certificate of\ncompletion of a course of study in first aid knowledge and skills pursu-\nant to subdivision one of Education Law Section 3001-b. Further, the\nindividual accompanying the coach must always be present with the coach\nduring extra-class athletic activities including but not limited to\npractices, scrimmages and during competition.\n\nTherefore, this bill ensures that people with physical disabilities that\nprevent them from performing CPR are not prevented from being a head\ncoach of a school athletic team due to their disability.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
